WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.820
I have to ask you about

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:04.780
what was the catalyst,

3
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:06.910
'cause you do have a child.

4
00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:08.710
That was the catalyst, like really.

5
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:10.463
It was like,

6
00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:12.770
how do I live with myself

7
00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:17.110
knowing that I am the example for this young person

8
00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:20.230
if I can't speak up for myself and for other people,

9
00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:24.380
especially in a time such as this that we are living in,

10
00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:26.650
when these things are getting pushed to the surface

11
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:29.050
and now is the time for truth and healing

12
00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:30.630
and having those hard conversations,

13
00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.333
and if I run away from this now,

14
00:00:34.005 --> 00:00:35.770
what do I tell my child?

15
00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:37.000
You know, be that person.

16
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.810
If you have the platform and the privilege

17
00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:40.000
to help other people,

18
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.570
dear God, use it.

19
00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:46.090
And I just felt I just had to do it.

20
00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:47.990
And I feel there should be exceptions

21
00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:49.410
to the statute of limitations

22
00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:50.727
because we're all sitting here going,

23
00:00:50.727 --> 00:00:52.390
"How do these people get away with it for so long?

24
00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:54.010
How are there so many victims?

25
00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:55.630
Why can't anything be done?"

26
00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:57.560
And it's because they've run out of time.

27
00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:00.410
And you know,

28
00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:03.180 line:15%
I am, for the past couple weeks,

29
00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.830 line:15%
been running around talking about this,

30
00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:05.850
promoting the documentary,

31
00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:07.550
but last night,

32
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:12.010
I did get home and break,

33
00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:15.920
because I've been running around having to be so strong

34
00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:17.850
and clear and concise.

35
00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:19.140
And you're sitting there,

36
00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.370
you've got all this pressure.

37
00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:23.880
You're the spokesperson for not just this documentary,

38
00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.520
but for all domestic violence survivors,

39
00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.810
and you're going, "Oh God, did I say it right?

40
00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:28.710
Did I word it right?

41
00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:29.990
What am I gonna get sued for?"

42
00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:33.530
Like, how is this gonna come back to hurt me?

43
00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:35.230
And then I stopped and thought

44
00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:38.860
I should not be this scared to tell the truth.

45
00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:40.700
And so the system is working,

46
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.170
but not the right system. (chuckles)

47
00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:44.780
And we've gotta find a balance

48
00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:48.800
to leave room for reform

49
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.910
but also give survivors this cushion that they need,

50
00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:54.140
especially when we know so much more about trauma now

51
00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:55.650
and how long it takes to process.

52
00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:58.560
Do you wanna take the Phoenix Act beyond California?

53
00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.930
Absolutely, and I feel like

54
00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:03.130
this will be a part of my life forever,

55
00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:04.490
and some people don't understand that,

56
00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:05.938
they think, "God, don't you wanna move on?

57
00:02:05.938 --> 00:02:06.940
Don't you wanna just stop

58
00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:08.540
and just never think about this again?"

59
00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:10.810
But it's like, by healing others,

60
00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:12.120
you also heal yourself,

61
00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:14.620
and it gives the pain a purpose.

62
00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:18.020
And if I can turn this into a healing moment

63
00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:20.350
and a moment for education and prevention

64
00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:22.640
and to shine some light on this issue

65
00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:25.700
that is severely under-reported and understood,

66
00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.474
then that brings me happiness,

67
00:02:27.474 --> 00:02:29.210
that brings me healing as well.

68
00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:33.310
I think that your documentary is such a game-changer

69
00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:38.450
for the reasons of helping people realize

70
00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:41.600
that trauma does take a long time to realize,

71
00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:43.930
for going out there and fighting

72
00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.220
and changing the legal system.

73
00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:48.000
I mean, I just have to say that

74
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.610
I think what I've learned about you

75
00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:56.250
is that you might be one of the best mothers

76
00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:59.580
I've ever seen in my life.
(Evan gasps)

77
00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:01.330
How you take everything

78
00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:03.790
that you've learned from your parents,

79
00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:06.120
how you've managed to heal with them,

80
00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:08.180
continue to work with them,

81
00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:11.970
see human beings for who they are,

82
00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:14.750
I have so much admiration for you.

83
00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:17.180
You are the living example

84
00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:20.340
of how a human being can function in this world.

85
00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:23.940
Process, protect others, tell their truth,

86
00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:25.940
you are my new hero.
Oh my God.

87
00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:28.500
I'm so honored that you would share

88
00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:30.420
in this experience for everybody,

89
00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:31.850
and you will change the world,

90
00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:33.360
and you will save lives from it.

91
00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:34.420
You really will.

92
00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:35.453
That's the goal, that's the goal.

93
00:03:35.453 --> 00:03:37.210
(audience claps)
That is the goal.

94
00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:38.993
There is, (chuckles)
(audience cheers)

95
00:03:38.993 --> 00:03:39.826
thanks.

96
00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:46.010
There's often a misconception

97
00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:47.760
with survivors of abuse

98
00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.908
that we are angry and just always out for revenge,

99
00:03:50.908 --> 00:03:52.950
and no,

100
00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:54.770
I really, really wanna approach this

101
00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:56.580
from a place of healing,

102
00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:59.130
and really, that is what we want.

103
00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.940
We want healing and accountability,

104
00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:04.400
and that's what we're asking for,

105
00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.310
and safety, (chuckles) you know?

106
00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.202
I think you're the fiercest!
Things that aren't too much

107
00:04:07.202 --> 00:04:08.247
to ask.
(audience claps)

108
00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:11.101
And you do, there's a levity to it.

109
00:04:11.101 --> 00:04:12.670
Thank you, Evan Rachel Wood.

